[843.273,"m","Destroy"]
[843.273,"o","$ "]
[843.273,"o","ov stack destroy -y --delete-data\r\n"]
[843.311,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what will be deleted from your Oracle Cloud tenancy (compartment ***):\r\n\r\n  # Everything the Terraform state in .openvidu/oracle holds: the master, the media nodes'\r\n  # instance pool, its instance configuration and its autoscaling configuration, the\r\n  # scale-in Function, its application and its log, their boot volumes, the network the\r\n  # stack created (its VCN, subnet, internet gateway, route table and security list) and\r\n  # its network security groups, the dynamic groups and the policies in the tenancy and\r\n  # the compartment, the bucket's Customer Secret Key, the SSH key's object in the bucket,\r\n  # not the vault: it is yours (--oci-vault), the bucket with the recordings and Meet\r\n  # data.\r\n  # Media nodes the scale-in detached from their pool are not in the state: the template's\r\n  # destroy finds them by their tags and terminates them, with oci and jq. Nothing drains\r\n  # then: the whole stack goes.\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/oracle init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/oracle destroy -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n--delete-data: the recordings and Meet data are in the Object Storage bucket: this deletes them.\r\nwarning: the vault is not the stack's (--oci-vault), so it stays, and this stack's secrets with it (its URL, its credentials, the license, the stack's access): schedule their deletion in the vault unless you need them\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[844.672,"o","\r\n▶ Delete the machines on Oracle Cloud…\r\n"]
